                                                <div id=3D"api_authenticati=
on" class=3D"tab-pane">
                                                    <div class=3D"api_doc">
                                                        <h2 class=3D"page-h=
eader">Authentication</h2>

                                                        <p>Calls that requi=
re authentication expect an HTTP header <i>Authorization</i> bearing a toke=
n, using the following format:</p>

                                                        <pre>Authorization:=
 Bearer <strong>your_api_token</strong></pre>
													=09
														<p>If you can not send an <i>Authorization</i> HTTP header yo=
u can also send your token as a parameter in REST API URLs, the parameter i=
s called <i>auth_token</i>:</p>

														<pre>/rest/1.0/method?auth_token=3D<strong>your_api_token</st=
rong></pre>
													=09
                                                        <p>This token can e=
ither be your <a href=3D"https://real-debrid.com/apitoken" target=3D"_blank=
">private API token</a>, or a token obtained using OAuth2's three-legged au=
thentication.</p>
                                                       =20
                                                        <p class=3D"alert a=
lert-warning"><strong>Warning:</strong> Never <strong>ever</strong> use you=
r private API token for public applications, it is insecure and gives acces=
s to all methods.</p>
                                                    </div>
												=09
                                                    <div class=3D"api_doc">
                                                        <h2 class=3D"page-h=
eader">Authentication for applications</h2>

                                                        <p>First, you must =
create an app in your control panel.</p>

                                                        <p>Once you have cr=
eated an app, you are provided a <b>client_id</b> and <b>client_secret</b> =
that you will use for the authentication process.</p>
                                                    </div>
												=09
													<div class=3D"api_doc">
                                                        <h2 class=3D"page-h=
eader">Opensource Apps</h2>

                                                        <p>You can use this=
 client ID on opensource apps if you don't need custom scopes or name:</p>
														<pre>X245A4XAIBGVM</pre>
													=09
														<p>This app is allowed on following scopes: unrestrict, torre=
nts, downloads, user</p>
														<p class=3D"alert alert-warning">This client ID can have stri=
cter limits than service limits due to poorly designed apps using it.</p>
													=09
                                                    </div>

                                                    <div class=3D"api_doc">
                                                        <h3>Which authentic=
ation process should you use?</h3>

                                                        <ul>
                                                            <li>If your app=
lication is a website: <a href=3D"https://api.real-debrid.com/#three_legged=
">three-legged OAuth2</a>.</li>
                                                            <li>If your app=
lication is a mobile app: <a href=3D"https://api.real-debrid.com/#device_au=
th">OAuth2 for devices</a>.</li>
                                                            <li>If your app=
lication is an opensource app or a script: <a href=3D"https://api.real-debr=
id.com/#device_auth_no_secret">OAuth2 for opensource apps</a>.</li>
                                                        </ul>
                                                    </div>

                                                    <div class=3D"api_doc" =
id=3D"three_legged">
                                                    	<p>The Base URL of the=
 OAuth2 API is:</p>
														<pre>https://api.real-debrid.com/oauth/v2/</pre>
                                                   =20
                                                        <h3>Workflow for we=
bsites or client applications</h3>

                                                        <p>This authenticat=
ion process uses three-legged OAuth2.</p>

                                                        <p>The following UR=
Ls are used in this process:</p>

                                                        <ul>
                                                            <li><b>authoriz=
e</b> endpoint: <i>/auth</i></li>
                                                            <li><b>token</b=
> endpoint: <i>/token</i></li>
                                                        </ul>

                                                        <p><i>Note: if your=
 application is not a website, you will have to make the user do these step=
s in a web view (e.g. UIWebView on iOS, WebView on Android=E2=80=A6).</i></=
p>

                                                        <h4>Full workflow</=
h4>

                                                        <ol>
                                                            <li>
                                                                <p>Your app=
lication redirects the user to Online.net's <b>authorize</b> endpoint, with=
 the following query string parameters:</p>
                                                                <ul>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>client_id</code>: your app's client_id</li>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>redirect_uri</code>: one of your application's redirect URLs (must be <a=
 href=3D"http://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_urlencode.asp" target=3D"_blank"=
>url encoded</a>)</li>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>response_type</code>: use the value "code"</li>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>state</code>: an arbitrary string that will be returned to your applicat=
ion, to help you check against CSRF</li>
                                                                </ul>

                                                                <h5>Example=
 URL for authorization:</h5>
                                                                <pre>https:=
//api.real-debrid.com/oauth/v2/auth?<b>client_id</b>=3DABCDEFGHIJKLM&amp;<b=
>redirect_uri</b>=3Dhttps%3A%2F%2Fexample.com&amp;<b>response_type</b>=3Dco=
de&amp;<b>state</b>=3Diloverd</pre>
                                                            </li>

                                                            <li>
                                                                <p>The user=
 chooses to authorize your application.</p>
                                                            </li>

                                                            <li>
                                                                <p>The user=
 gets redirected to the URL you specified using the parameter <i>redirect_u=
ri</i>, with the following query string parameters:</p>
                                                                <ul>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>code</code>: the code that you will use to get a token</li>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>state</code>: the same value that you sent earlier</li>
                                                                </ul>
                                                            </li>

                                                            <li>
                                                                <p>Using th=
e value of <i>code</i>, your application makes a direct POST request (not i=
n the user's browser) to the <b>token</b> endpoint, with the following para=
meters:</p>
                                                                <ul>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>client_id</code></li>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>client_secret</code></li>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>code</code>: the value that you received earlier</li>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>redirect_uri</code>: one of your application's redirect URLs</li>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>grant_type</code>: use the value "authorization_code"</li>
                                                                </ul>

                                                                <h5>Example=
 cURL call to obtain an access token:</h5>
                                                                <pre>curl -=
X POST "https://api.real-debrid.com/oauth/v2/token" -d "<b>client_id</b>=3D=
ABCDEFGHIJKLM&amp;<b>client_secret</b>=3Dabcdefghsecret0123456789&amp;<b>co=
de</b>=3DABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789&amp;<b>redirect_uri</b>=3Dhtt=
ps://your-app.tld/realdebrid_api&amp;<b>grant_type</b>=3Dauthorization_code=
"</pre>
                                                            </li>

                                                            <li>
                                                                <p>If every=
thing is correct, the access token is returned as a JSON object with the fo=
llowing properties:</p>
                                                                <ul>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>access_token</code></li>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>expires_in</code>: token validity period, in seconds</li>
                                                                    <li><co=
de>token_type</code>: "Bearer"</li>
																	<li><code>refresh_token</code>: token that only expires wh=
en your application rights are revoked by user</li>
                                                                </ul>
                                                            </li>

                                                            <li>
                                                                <p>Your app=
lication stores the access token and uses it for the user's subsequent visi=
ts.</p>
																<p>Your application must also stores the refresh token that=
 will be used to get new access tokens once their validity period is expire=
d.</p>
                                                            </li>
                                                        </ol>
                                                    </div>

                                                    <div class=3D"api_doc" =
id=3D"device_auth">
                                                        <h3>Workflow for mo=
bile apps</h3>

                                                        <p>This authenticat=
ion process uses a variant of OAuth2, tailored for mobile devices.</p>

                                                        <p>The following UR=
Ls are used in this process:</p>

                                                        <ul>
                                                            <li><b>device</=
b> endpoint: <i>/device/code</i></li>
                                                            <li><b>token</b=
> endpoint: <i>/token</i></li>
                                                        </ul>

                                                        <p><i>Note: you may=
 have to make the user do some steps in a web view (e.g. UIWebView on iOS, =
WebView on Android=E2=80=A6) if you want to do all these steps from the mob=
ile app.</i></p>

                                                        <h4>Full workflow</=
h4>

